From 023b9d1c55c3fefd3147a825bfb388db639ce8fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 16:14:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 148/188] PCI/PM: Remove the device from the PME poll list in
 pci_destroy_dev()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pci_stop_dev() removes the device from the PME poll list before
releasing its driver, but the device can end up back on it: a runtime
suspend racing with the driver release re-enables PME polling through
pci_finish_runtime_suspend(), and for a surprise-removed device the
balancing disable on the resume side never runs. The stale list entry
then outlives the device, and the next pci_pme_list_scan() dereferences
freed memory:

  BUG: unable to handle page fault for address: 0000000b00000040
  Workqueue: events_freezable pci_pme_list_scan
  RIP: 0010:pci_pme_list_scan+0x40/0x210

Observed on the MSI Claw 8 EX AI+: its SD Express slot hot-removes the
RTS5264 card reader, a PME polling device, whenever a card muxes the
reader off the bus, and the reader is usually runtime suspended at that
point.

Remove the device from the poll list again in pci_destroy_dev() after
device_del() has permanently shut runtime PM down, so nothing can
re-enable polling afterwards.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Signed-off-by: Nícolas F. R. A. Prado <nfraprado@collabora.com>
---
 drivers/pci/remove.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/remove.c b/drivers/pci/remove.c
index d8bffa214..4e3e11a4c 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/remove.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/remove.c
@@ -45,6 +45,13 @@ static void pci_destroy_dev(struct pci_dev *dev)
 
 	device_del(&dev->dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * pci_stop_dev() already left the PME poll list, but a runtime
+	 * suspend racing with the driver release can put the device back
+	 * on it. Runtime PM is permanently off now, so leave it for good.
+	 */
+	pci_pme_active(dev, false);
+
 	down_write(&pci_bus_sem);
 	list_del(&dev->bus_list);
 	up_write(&pci_bus_sem);
-- 
2.55.0

